123
STS-72 Preparation - RSS roll back
1/10/96

The Rotating Service Structure (RSS) is rolled back at 
Launch Pad 39B to reveal in full the Space Shuttle 
Endeavour.  Rollback of the RSS marks another major 
milestone in the approximately three-day-long Shuttle launch 
countdown process.  Endeavour is being prepared for liftoff 
on the first Shuttle flight of 1996, Mission STS-72, at 4:18 
am EST, January 11.  Behind the shuttle, water gushes from 
the Sound Suppression system tank as it is topped off, a 
procedure that also is performed in preparation for launch.

